# Pivot SACCO — gateway Caddy when another proxy already terminates TLS.
# The production compose file still starts Caddy with /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.
# Point the container at this file only when host Caddy (or another proxy)
# owns 443 and forwards plain HTTP here.
#
# Routing is in routes.caddy. /alerts/* is not defined in this container:
# the alerts process is on the host at 127.0.0.1:8095. See
# alerts/deploy/caddy-alerts.caddy. Do not reload the incomplete host
# file /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.

:80 {
	import routes.caddy
}
